.vercel

# NOTE: dist/ is intentionally committed. vercel.json uses the legacy
# `builds` config pointing directly at dist/server.js -- Vercel does not
# run a build step for it, so the compiled output must already be in
# git. Previously having "dist" here silently hid whole new modules
# (skills, reviews) from git, causing "Cannot find module" crashes in
# production. Always run `npm run build` and commit dist/ before pushing.